{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\epsilon : \\mathcal{P}_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\mathcal{P}_0 = \\mathcal{A}[\\mathcal{B}],\\quad\n\\mathcal{P}_1 = \\mathcal{A}[\\mathcal{A}[\\mathcal{B}]],\\quad \\ldots\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-standard-resolution-sheaves-rings}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a5c5828a2f244e8a489525f2824ab60b03ba2ba53a425934ecd11da601d3105f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:723d0ba634d2f54233e470595dcb3e412347a9577970d1ef1c1fca930b4ff2f6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings\non <MATH_0003>. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>standard resolution of <MATH_0004> over\n<MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the augmentation\n<MATH_0006>\nwith terms\n<MATH_0007>\nand maps as constructed above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d1f17288385b4ff243037ebeb91921b3b60b035d6c11f0dd219efd6479fa7613", "unit_id": "tag:08SR:statement"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-section-differentials}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1c99816a7ed39a5614ce948707b35fa5a341e68e509aa58950c9d94538d688d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWith this definition in hand the cotangent complex of a map of sheaves\nof rings is defined as follows.\nWe will use the module of differentials as defined in\nModules on Sites, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9739adcecd39921e0b45f2846da909f3701462acdc4ea04ab65a1fa3229751c0", "unit_id": "tag:08UQ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$L_{\\mathcal{B}/\\mathcal{A}}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Omega_{\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet/\\mathcal{A}}\n\\otimes_{\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet, \\epsilon} \\mathcal{B}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\epsilon : \\mathcal{P}_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0010": "$L_{\\mathcal{B}/\\mathcal{A}}$", "MATH_0011": "$D(\\mathcal{B})$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-cotangent-complex-morphism-sheaves-rings}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6fc1296d4dba68f5065c43b21cdbb9e1fde7386916a9ce09512c7b0160028045", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d57d15bfe95fd38c47dfda58533f1918a1aca60aefa5828a55856aa1d7dfe338", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings\non <MATH_0003>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cotangent complex<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0004>\nis the complex of <MATH_0005>-modules associated to the\nsimplicial module\n<MATH_0006>\nwhere <MATH_0007>\nis the standard resolution of <MATH_0008> over\n<MATH_0009>. We usually think of <MATH_0010>\nas an object of <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:882af533c59c7c709ccfbc442973a7bf19ade6635d3f94fb25a16761377d01d6", "unit_id": "tag:08SS:statement"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08UQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-commutative-square-sheaves}\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{B} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{B}' \\\\\n\\mathcal{A} \\ar[u] \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{A}' \\ar[u]\n}\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nL_{\\mathcal{B}/\\mathcal{A}} \\longrightarrow L_{\\mathcal{B}'/\\mathcal{A}'}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{P}'_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{B}'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{B}'$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{A}'$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{P}'_\\bullet$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{P}_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{P}'_\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{B}'$", "MATH_0015": "$$\n\\mathcal{P}_0 = \\mathcal{A}[\\mathcal{B}]\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{A}'[\\mathcal{B}'] = \\mathcal{P}'_0,\n\\quad\n\\mathcal{P}_1 = \\mathcal{A}[\\mathcal{A}[\\mathcal{B}]]\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{A}'[\\mathcal{A}'[\\mathcal{B}']] = \\mathcal{P}'_1\n$$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{A}'$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{B}'$", "MATH_0018": "$L_{\\mathcal{B}/\\mathcal{A}} \\to L_{\\mathcal{B}'/\\mathcal{A}'}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-functoriality}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d83fd6c130c37e666763e217b8693ca82d5fed1357a6ad937d1171bac494f72b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f1810434619ab65f2722d4a2ac450344afca18a8e73c8a8a83ff127d4b131889", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThese constructions satisfy a functoriality similar to that discussed\nin Section <REF_0001>. Namely, given a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof sheaves of rings on <MATH_0002> there is a canonical\n<MATH_0003>-linear map of complexes\n<MATH_0004>\nconstructed as follows. If <MATH_0005> is the\nstandard resolution of <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007> and\n<MATH_0008> is the\nstandard resolution of <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010>,\nthen there is a canonical map <MATH_0011>\nof simplicial <MATH_0012>-algebras compatible with the augmentations\n<MATH_0013> and\n<MATH_0014>. The maps\n<MATH_0015>\nand so on are given by the given maps <MATH_0016>\nand <MATH_0017>. The desired map\n<MATH_0018>\nthen comes from the associated maps on sheaves of differentials.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fcb2a2313850eca7d0fa26662fbe2d776d551f84255380df3e20abd3069d959", "unit_id": "tag:08UQ:prose-0003"}
